WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.912
After Fritz had added another seat to his kayak, we were ready to gather oysters.

2
00:00:04.913 --> 00:00:07.274
Jack rode with Fritz in the kayak.

3
00:00:07.275 --> 00:00:11.330
Mother and Franz stayed behind while Ernest joined me on the sailboat.

4
00:00:11.331 --> 00:00:15.857
We arrived in beautiful Pearl Bay, where we worked hard for two days.

5
00:00:15.858 --> 00:00:19.447
The following morning Fritz led us out of the bay.

6
00:00:19.448 --> 00:00:22.435
Jack and Ernest were busy with the sails.

7
00:00:22.436 --> 00:00:27.801
So they did not notice when Fritz waved to me and turned his kayak in the opposite direction.

8
00:00:27.802 --> 00:00:30.843
I watched him quickly vanish behind a point.

9
00:00:30.844 --> 00:00:33.623
"Where's Fritz?" Jack asked suddenly.

10
00:00:33.624 --> 00:00:36.876
"He wanted to explore more of the coast," I said.

11
00:00:36.877 --> 00:00:41.192
"If he finds something interesting, he may be gone for two or three days."

12
00:00:41.193 --> 00:00:44.345
The boys accepted my explanation without question.

13
00:00:44.346 --> 00:00:47.813
That evening we sailed into our own Safety Bay.

14
00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:51.482
Five days passed and Fritz still had not returned.

15
00:00:51.483 --> 00:00:56.477
I tried to hide my anxiety but finally decided that we should go looking for him.

16
00:00:56.478 --> 00:00:58.986
Everyone was delighted at the idea.

17
00:00:58.987 --> 00:01:02.404
Even my wife agreed to accompany us in the sailboat.

18
00:01:02.405 --> 00:01:06.269
Our beautiful little boat bounded over the water in the bright sunshine.

19
00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:11.089
We were almost at Pearl Bay when I saw a dark mass just under the water.

20
00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:13.193
"That's a big rock," I said.

21
00:01:13.194 --> 00:01:15.601
"There's another one!" shouted Jack.

22
00:01:15.602 --> 00:01:18.807
" That rock is moving!" cried

23
00:01:18.808 --> 00:01:22.496
Franz. "That's not a rock," said Ernest. "That's a

24
00:01:22.497 --> 00:01:26.249
whale!" We watched as the whales rose from the water around

25
00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:29.231
us. "They're coming up to breathe," Ernest

26
00:01:29.232 --> 00:01:34.304
explained. Suddenly Jack grabbed my arm. "Father, look over there. Near that

27
00:01:34.305 --> 00:01:38.717
rock." I glanced over just in time to see a native hiding his canoe behind a

28
00:01:38.718 --> 00:01:42.429
rock. The man stood up for a moment and peered intently at

29
00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:44.509
us. Then he ducked behind the

30
00:01:44.510 --> 00:01:48.278
rock. A moment later he came out and started paddling toward

31
00:01:48.279 --> 00:01:51.321
us. "Hoist a white flag to show we're friendly," I

32
00:01:51.322 --> 00:01:53.381
ordered. "And hand me the

33
00:01:53.382 --> 00:01:58.949
megaphone." I seized the megaphone and uttered the few friendly words I knew in the Malay

34
00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:02.737
language. But neither my words nor the white flag produced the right

35
00:02:02.738 --> 00:02:06.303
effect. The native turned his boat and headed back toward

36
00:02:06.304 --> 00:02:08.958
shore. Jack lost patience and grabbed the

37
00:02:08.959 --> 00:02:11.671
megaphone. "Come here and make friends with us or

38
00:02:11.672 --> 00:02:14.000
we'll—" "Stop! Stop!" I

39
00:02:14.001 --> 00:02:18.034
cried. "You will only alarm the man with your wild words and gestures."

40
00:02:18.035 --> 00:02:22.641
"But look, Father," said Jack. "He's paddling straight for us again."

41
00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:26.433
"The villain has Fritz's kayak!" said Franz.

42
00:02:26.434 --> 00:02:29.524
Among the boys only Ernest remained calm.

43
00:02:29.525 --> 00:02:33.179
He took the megaphone from Jack and addressed the man in the kayak.

44
00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:35.588
"Welcome aboard, Fritz!" he said.

45
00:02:35.589 --> 00:02:39.673
No sooner were the words out of his mouth than we all recognized Fritz.

46
00:02:39.674 --> 00:02:43.218
In a few more minutes he was on board the sailboat.

47
00:02:43.219 --> 00:02:46.983
Mother threw her arms around him as we peppered him with questions.

48
00:02:46.984 --> 00:02:49.383
"Where have you been?" asked Jack.

49
00:02:49.384 --> 00:02:52.949
"Why have you been gone so long?" asked Franz.

50
00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:56.032
"Why were you hiding from us?" demanded Ernest.

51
00:02:56.033 --> 00:02:59.172
"Slow down." Fritz laughed.

52
00:02:59.173 --> 00:03:02.460
"I never dreamed you'd come after me in the sailboat.

53
00:03:02.461 --> 00:03:04.945
I thought you must be Malay pirates.

54
00:03:04.946 --> 00:03:08.885
When you addressed me in that language, I was sure you were pirates!

55
00:03:08.886 --> 00:03:11.199
But then I recognized Jack."

56
00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:14.189
"Do you know a good spot where we can anchor?" I asked.

57
00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:18.050
"I can lead you to an island where there is a splendid place to anchor."

58
00:03:18.051 --> 00:03:20.481
He gave me a glance full of meaning.

59
00:03:20.482 --> 00:03:24.670
"The island itself contains all sorts of interesting things."

60
00:03:24.671 --> 00:03:29.271
Now that I knew Fritz's expedition had succeeded, it was time to tell my wife.

61
00:03:29.272 --> 00:03:34.857
When she heard about the Englishwoman's message, she was almost overcome with emotion.

62
00:03:34.858 --> 00:03:40.361
"Another human being—another woman!—here with us," she said.

63
00:03:40.362 --> 00:03:43.355
"But why didn't you tell me about her before this?"

64
00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:47.145
"I didn't want to raise your hopes until I was sure," I replied.

65
00:03:47.146 --> 00:03:53.837
It was difficult to conceal our excitement from the boys, who sensed that something was about to happen.

66
00:03:53.838 --> 00:03:58.082
As soon as the anchor was dropped, they eagerly sprang ashore.

67
00:03:58.083 --> 00:04:00.715
We all followed Fritz in silence.

68
00:04:00.716 --> 00:04:05.080
Suddenly the trail ended in front of a shelter made of tree branches.

69
00:04:05.081 --> 00:04:07.745
A cheerful fire burned in front of it.

70
00:04:07.746 --> 00:04:11.501
Fritz dove into the shelter, leaving his brothers behind.

71
00:04:11.502 --> 00:04:16.712
In another moment he emerged, leading a small, handsome youth by the hand.

72
00:04:16.713 --> 00:04:21.301
From his clothing, the young man appeared to be an officer in the English navy.

73
00:04:21.302 --> 00:04:26.895
Radiant with joy, Fritz said, "I would like to introduce Edward Montrose.

74
00:04:26.896 --> 00:04:30.511
Please welcome him into our family circle as a friend and a brother."

75
00:04:30.512 --> 00:04:32.435
I stared at the young man.

76
00:04:32.436 --> 00:04:39.009
For some reason the Englishwoman wanted us to think she was a man.

